; lisp: format-clauses.lisp
; The collector's halt from FORMAT's clause buffer (sys/io/format.lisp,
; FORMAT-RECLAIM-CLAUSES; lisp/format-clauses.lisp), planted at 2 M words of
; main memory: run it only when named, on a machine of 2 M words
; (--main-memory-size 2MW through a --quux wrapper); at more nothing is
; forced out and the first case fails.  FORMAT's temporary consing goes to an
; area of the check's own; a call with three clauses gives their strings back
; with the area's free pointer on a page boundary; that page is forced out;
; a call with one clause conses its string at the boundary, so the page comes
; back fresh (CONSF's M-DONT-SWAP-IN) and the second clause's string is gone;
; then a collection.  A buffer that still points to that string makes the
; scavenger transport it, and %FIND-STRUCTURE-HEADER's scan back from it meets
; the first string's GC-FORWARD words: ILLOP, HALT-CONS from XFSHS1+2, and the
; machine stops (no answer to the collection case).  Run with
;   --compile --files sys/io/format.lisp,tools/system-check/lisp/format-clauses.lisp
; The planting cases are the controls: they pass with and without the change.
; System 2002 (handover-2002-a07a05c) and System 2001 without the change halt
; in the collection case (measured).
; the generational collector (contract G3 step 2, Q-GCa) turns automatic
; collection on at boot; its flips, a tenured one after the large arrays below
; above all, move what this check plants (measured on step 2's first band:
; the planted area's region was freed, and fc-plant-2 met an address "in no
; region").  Off first, as revision 14's band had it.
(progn (when si:gc-on (si:gc-off)) si:gc-on) => NIL
(<= (si:system-communication-area si:%sys-com-memory-size) (* 2 1024 1024)) => T
(format::fc-plant-1) => T
(format::fc-plant-2) => (T T 0)
(format::fc-collect) => T
(format nil "~[a~;b~]" 1) => "b"
